This file gathers and re-exports the specialization order, the lower subbasic sets of elements not below a given element, the principal up-sets, and the predicate that a topology is coarser than the Scott topology. These are the ingredients of Scott's March 1972 correction: Milner observed that a T0-topology on a complete lattice need not make every open set Scott-open, the two extreme T0-topologies inducing the order are generated by those subbasic sets, and the corrected proofs of Propositions 2.9, 2.10, and 3.3 assume every open of the given topology is Scott-open. For Proposition 2.10 the retraction of a directed set in a retract sends the ambient join to the join in the retract, and function-space joins are pointwise, so the product topology sits inside the Scott topology once that hypothesis holds.
